Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.64,0:00:09.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Understood, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.09,0:00:16.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Your right to succeed the \Nthrone has been restored?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.90,0:00:21.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There was no other choice, with Al gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.73,0:00:24.12,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Um, so... This means...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.12,0:00:27.83,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,You'll be the next ruler of the kingdom?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.83,0:00:29.28,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.49,0:00:32.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The kingdom's never had \Na queen in charge, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.00,0:00:34.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The king's spouse has always \Nbeen just a consort...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.74,0:00:38.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So I guess I'll have to take \Na prince consort eventually.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.35,0:00:39.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A prince consort?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.85,0:00:42.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I have to pass down \Nthe royal blood, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.51,0:00:50.85,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,We've still got the much bigger problem \Nof getting the nobles to accept me, though!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.85,0:00:53.71,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Even after the right to the throne \Nhas been restored to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.14,0:00:54.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.43,0:00:59.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No matter how far I get, not being \Nable to use magic holds me back.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.69,0:01:03.99,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I think I can be of some help.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.17,0:01:07.61,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,As the daughter of Duke Magenta,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.61,0:01:10.74,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I should be able to serve as an intermediary \Nbetween you and the nobles.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.74,0:01:11.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.93,0:01:15.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This doesn't really have \Nanything to do with you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.29,0:01:16.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can just take it easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.93,0:01:19.13,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,N-Nothing to do with...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.71,0:01:22.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie's my assistant \Nin magicology research,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.24,0:01:25.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and Lainie, I guess you're \Na maid-in-training.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.10,0:01:28.28,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This whole issue is totally \Nseparate from any of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.53,0:01:31.69,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, I'm gonna head to the workshop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.08,0:01:40.52,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I thought you would argue \Nagainst what she just said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.77,0:01:42.37,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.73,0:01:46.56,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I mean... if Miss Anis \Ntakes a consort... well...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.12,0:01:49.28,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I was...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.86,0:01:53.12,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,asked by Prince Algard \Nto take care of Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.71,0:01:57.84,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I have to support her \Nas one of her subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.45,0:02:02.61,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I... see...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.13,0:02:20.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay. I was prepared for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.00,0:02:22.70,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I know I can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.59,0:02:26.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I am Anisphia Wynn Palettia,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.33,0:02:29.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,the only princess in this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.38,0:02:31.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It can't be helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.11,0:02:37.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.13,0:02:39.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.59,0:04:09.97,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:04:01.59,0:04:09.97,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.59,0:04:09.97,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.05,0:04:14.44,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Honestly, she's such an idiot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.44,0:04:17.52,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,She should just adopt a kid from \Nsome prominent noble family.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.79,0:04:20.24,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Th-There's no need to put it that way...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.24,0:04:24.46,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Are you concerned about \NMiss Anis becoming queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.46,0:04:25.65,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.65,0:04:29.76,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Aren't {\i1}you{\i0} the one who should be concerned?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.76,0:04:32.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, not in particular...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.54,0:04:35.50,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Be honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.07,0:04:37.70,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am being honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.21,0:04:42.64,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's only right for me to support \Nthe queen as one of her subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.63,0:04:44.50,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Look—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.50,0:04:46.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm back!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.13,0:04:50.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Er, huh? You're not done with the exam yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.36,0:04:51.05,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Hah!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.74,0:04:57.02,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Did you have a nice time \Ntalking to all those nobles?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.74,0:05:00.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, uh... I mean, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.48,0:05:03.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I might actually be better \Nat this than I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.95,0:05:05.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,kinda?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.42,0:05:09.24,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What is that look on your face?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.24,0:05:11.25,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,C-Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.25,0:05:13.19,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Insulting my face is uncalled for.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.19,0:05:14.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That card's off-limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.04,0:05:18.46,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You know very well that's not what I meant!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.74,0:05:21.96,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just know what my own face \Nlooks like, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.96,0:05:25.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So long, old me! Say hello to my new normal!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.08,0:05:27.88,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A new you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.88,0:05:30.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm Anisphia Wynn Palettia,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.80,0:05:33.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,the princess who's next \Nin line for the throne!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.85,0:05:42.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.91,0:05:45.85,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Tilty, please, that's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.07,0:05:47.82,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.21,0:05:49.78,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You are {\i1}such{\i0} an idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.20,0:05:53.82,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If that's how you're going to be, \Ndon't blame me for whatever happens!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.83,0:06:11.85,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,So this is where you've been.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.80,0:06:16.26,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh... Sorry about earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.74,0:06:21.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was trying to avoid seeing Tilty \Nbecause I knew it'd end up this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.20,0:06:21.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,No, it's...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.06,0:06:23.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Don't worry about her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.29,0:06:27.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's not really fun when she gets mad \Nat me over my face, though...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.16,0:06:30.48,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.48,0:06:31.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.02,0:06:33.82,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What Tilty said was completely out of line,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.82,0:06:36.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,but you two seemed to be on the same page.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.58,0:06:43.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,O-Oh, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.05,0:06:46.71,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,More importantly, I gotta go \Npick up Arc-en-Ciel!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.95,0:06:49.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,A-Arc-en-Ciel?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.16,0:06:50.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was too hard on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.80,0:06:54.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so I left it with a blacksmith \Nin town for maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.13,0:06:56.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, see you later!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.98,0:07:00.99,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's late. You can do that tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.99,0:07:02.97,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And I'll be going with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.97,0:07:03.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.47,0:07:07.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Your body is not yours alone anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.49,0:07:09.69,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If you wait until something happens, \Nit'll be too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.61,0:07:15.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you... talking about a date?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.16,0:07:17.04,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.04,0:07:19.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just the two of us, sneaking out on a date?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.99,0:07:22.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Just us?! What about guards?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.38,0:07:24.96,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If we guard each other, there's no problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.96,0:07:27.16,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's... But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.01,0:07:33.09,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come on, Euphie...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.10,0:07:34.97,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.21,0:07:47.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This way, Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.43,0:07:49.47,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.47,0:07:52.36,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I mean, um... Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.55,0:07:55.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Get used to it quick, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.12,0:08:02.33,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,You're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.83,0:08:06.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, Tomas. All done with \Nthe weapon I left here?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.30,0:08:07.94,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Of course I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.26,0:08:12.26,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Who's she?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.67,0:08:14.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,My assistant!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.96,0:08:15.83,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.38,0:08:18.71,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,The one who uses that thing, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.39,0:08:22.34,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Pleasure to meet you. My name is Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.17,0:08:26.06,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I know who you are. Duke Magenta's daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.48,0:08:30.16,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,The fiancée Miss Anis swiped \Nfrom Prince Algard, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.16,0:08:32.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No, no! I didn't swipe her!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.20,0:08:35.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,We were both in agreement! \NIt was a completely legal procedure!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.44,0:08:38.63,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I couldn't care less about \Nwhat nobles are up to.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.72,0:08:44.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Who you see here right now is just Euphie, \Nso please call me that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.17,0:08:48.67,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,That so? Doesn't sound so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.93,0:08:50.12,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Hang on just a sec.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.33,0:08:57.06,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Pull it out, and check it over.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.72,0:09:16.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, is something...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.60,0:09:19.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,My assistant's pretty amazing, isn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.28,0:09:21.42,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.99,0:09:26.23,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I can see why you took a liking to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.52,0:09:31.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,By now, I'm so dependent on Arc-en-Ciel \Nthat I don't feel right without it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.02,0:09:35.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you for your flawless work, Tomas.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.72,0:09:37.08,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Yeah, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.60,0:09:45.47,Default,Old Man,0,0,0,,Oh! It's the real Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.47,0:09:47.78,Default,Lady,0,0,0,,See? I told you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.78,0:09:50.30,Default,Shopkeeper,0,0,0,,Miss Anis! I got some nice, \Nfresh fish in today!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.30,0:09:50.93,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.93,0:09:53.41,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Let's finish the game we started last time!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.54,0:09:56.64,Default,Crowd,0,0,0,,Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.64,0:09:57.96,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Come on, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.76,0:10:01.04,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.44,0:10:05.23,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I'll just do some final checks on this \Nand then give it to Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.93,0:10:09.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Sorry! I won't be long!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.10,0:10:12.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come on, take turns!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.00,0:10:20.63,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Tell me one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.05,0:10:22.34,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.33,0:10:26.34,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Will our next ruler be Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.84,0:10:31.75,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I believe so, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.27,0:10:34.60,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.60,0:10:38.97,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Are you that uneasy with the idea \Nof Miss Anis being queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.44,0:10:42.25,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I'm not uneasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.25,0:10:45.32,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,She comes to visit the town \Npretty frequently.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.08,0:10:50.44,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,There are a lot of folks who \Nbelieve she can be trusted.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.01,0:10:54.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But you don't seem very happy about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.62,0:10:56.48,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Yeah, I'm not.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.48,0:10:57.70,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.92,0:11:00.49,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,You have no ide—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.43,0:11:03.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Look at all the stuff they gave me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.48,0:11:05.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can have some of it, Tomas.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.06,0:11:09.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Did something happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.36,0:11:12.22,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Nope. We're done talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.52,0:11:14.62,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Go on home.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.35,0:11:29.34,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.66,0:11:31.34,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.79,0:11:33.74,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.74,0:11:34.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.26,0:11:39.03,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You've seemed out of sorts \Nsince you returned from town.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.12,0:11:44.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm just... not sure I understand anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.75,0:11:53.38,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I really believe that Miss Anis \Nwill be a queen
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.38,0:11:56.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,who can bring the nobles and \Nthe commoners together...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.47,0:12:00.64,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Don't you think so, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.86,0:12:03.12,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I think she will be a benevolent ruler.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.19,0:12:05.25,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.79,0:12:07.65,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She probably isn't cut out for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.79,0:12:13.08,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Having power and being forced \Nto use it are not the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.58,0:12:15.66,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If the princess becomes queen,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.66,0:12:19.41,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,she won't be able to go into \Ntown anymore, will she?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.63,0:12:20.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.56,0:12:24.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But she has a responsibility,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.44,0:12:26.49,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,so I suppose she has no choice...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.15,0:12:31.04,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Come with me, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.58,0:12:49.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Did Miss Anis do all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.12,0:12:55.37,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The princess may act like a wild child \Nwith no concept of good sense,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.37,0:12:58.96,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,but at her core, she is a \Nvery conscientious person.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.96,0:13:01.18,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That is true, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.08,0:13:05.00,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,In order to be a ruler accepted by all,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.55,0:13:08.76,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,she will probably never associate \Nwith magicology again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.06,0:13:10.54,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.22,0:13:13.62,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,She takes too much upon herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.20,0:13:16.69,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,That hasn't changed since she was little.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.09,0:13:18.71,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If she becomes queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.02,0:13:23.60,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,she will most likely throw away \Nwhat is precious to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.42,0:13:29.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.79,0:13:33.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am the daughter of Duke Magenta.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.67,0:13:37.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I have my duty as a noble... \Nas part of a royal household.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.32,0:13:40.92,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Once the princess has fulfilled her duty...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.62,0:13:46.85,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Do you think she will smile happily?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.18,0:13:54.40,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That... That's not...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.32,0:13:58.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But... why...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.50,0:14:00.53,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,do I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.23,0:14:11.37,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.87,0:14:14.39,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Not knowing what else to do,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.39,0:14:17.17,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,you came all the way here to talk to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.50,0:14:18.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.82,0:14:25.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I just... want to help her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.56,0:14:28.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't want to see her sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.56,0:14:33.00,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It just hurts so much that I can't solve \NMiss Anis's problems for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.43,0:14:37.65,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,"Miss Anis's problems"?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.90,0:14:40.11,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,That's your first mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.27,0:14:41.33,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.87,0:14:45.03,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,This is actually {\i1}your{\i0} problem, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.79,0:14:47.47,Default,Euphie,0,0,0,,Mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.47,0:14:50.06,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Yes, an issue of your own feelings.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.32,0:14:52.87,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What are you really thinking right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.59,0:14:57.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Say it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.35,0:15:00.65,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.00,0:15:02.38,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.43,0:15:06.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's my duty to support the royal family,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.69,0:15:09.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,but I personally...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.01,0:15:17.15,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,don't want Miss Anis to become queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.98,0:15:24.95,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Having your heart at odds with \Nyour duty was painful, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.39,0:15:30.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I know this feeling I have is wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.07,0:15:34.70,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What does it matter \Nwhether it's right or wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.65,0:15:41.88,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Just try to find the path \Nthat you truly want to take.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.42,0:15:46.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Can I really... have hope?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.24,0:15:49.50,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If that's what you've decided to do,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.50,0:15:51.79,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,there's no one who can stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.53,0:15:56.50,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You're the most brilliant genius young lady \Nin this kingdom, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.64,0:16:10.33,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It's unusual for you to visit my office,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.63,0:16:11.57,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.03,0:16:14.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,There's something I wish \Nto consult you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.43,0:16:17.25,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Oh? That's even more unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.65,0:16:24.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Does the kingdom's next ruler \Nabsolutely have to be Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.33,0:16:28.79,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Why do you ask that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.75,0:16:35.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Because I don't want Miss Anis to be queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.02,0:16:44.14,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,A kingdom is only a kingdom \Nif it has a monarch.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.64,0:16:50.12,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Princess Anisphia must fulfill her duty \Nin order to protect this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.12,0:16:53.19,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,And it's your job to support her.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.19,0:16:54.19,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Am I wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.14,0:16:56.52,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.73,0:17:02.95,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Even so, I cannot accept it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.23,0:17:04.12,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.59,0:17:07.83,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Because that is not where \NMiss Anis can truly smile!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.39,0:17:12.35,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Smile?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.76,0:17:16.05,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Are you saying that's more important \Nthan our kingdom's future?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.49,0:17:20.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This kingdom, and all of its people,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.52,0:17:24.35,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,cannot be traded for just one \Nperson's smile. I realize that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.54,0:17:26.89,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But still...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.11,0:17:29.36,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't want to accept it as \Njust the way things must be!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.55,0:17:35.99,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Is this out of devotion or obligation?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.99,0:17:37.94,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Or is it sympathy?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.42,0:17:43.62,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I just... love her.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.32,0:17:49.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Even if I lose my position, my family, \Nand everything I have,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.93,0:17:51.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,my feelings won't change.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.17,0:17:57.25,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You truly care that much \Nfor Princess Anisphia?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.86,0:17:59.72,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.26,0:18:05.20,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,As Duke Magenta,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.20,0:18:08.36,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I cannot, under any circumstances, \Naccept these misplaced feelings of yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.87,0:18:12.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.31,0:18:16.23,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But while I am fully aware \Nthat it isn't right,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.23,0:18:17.39,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can no longer...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.71,0:18:30.58,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Long ago, Orphanse loved gardening \Nmore than anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.19,0:18:36.13,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,He even declared that his dream was to \Nbecome a common subject and study plants.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.13,0:18:39.99,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,He was no less of a problem child \Nthan Princess Anisphia herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.57,0:18:44.22,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,But he threw away his dream of happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.22,0:18:47.90,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,All to stop the nobles' uprising \Nand become king.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.90,0:18:50.28,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,And I supported him with all my strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.90,0:18:52.41,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,For our kingdom's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.90,0:18:56.08,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.57,0:19:01.78,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,The truth is, at that time, \Nwe had another option.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.50,0:19:03.75,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.79,0:19:13.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Spirits? But why...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.60,0:19:33.95,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I wish you wouldn't show up without notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.90,0:19:36.64,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,It's been a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.63,0:19:40.11,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You've aged quite a bit, Grantz.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.11,0:19:42.59,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,And you don't seem to have changed at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.05,0:19:44.96,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,What brings you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.96,0:19:47.06,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You've already figured it out, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.06,0:19:48.92,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Aren't you going to introduce me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.93,0:19:53.37,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,This lady...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.37,0:19:55.85,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,is Miss Lumi, a spirit contractor.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.60,0:19:58.71,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Spirit contractor?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.16,0:20:05.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um... Shall I leave you two alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.19,0:20:07.20,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Oh, my, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.76,0:20:10.43,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,I came here to see {\i1}you{\i0}, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.77,0:20:11.65,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.15,0:20:14.10,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Tell me, Euphyllia...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.48,0:20:18.56,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,What does a spirit contract \Nsignify in this kingdom?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.83,0:20:21.03,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Eh? Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.27,0:20:25.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Forging a contract with a greater spirit \Nthat possesses immense power
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.51,0:20:28.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,signifies one's authority \Nas a member of the royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.71,0:20:34.15,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,From the legend of the founder \Nand first king of Palettia, yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.41,0:20:37.13,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Those who have entered a spirit contract
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.13,0:20:39.95,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,are capable of starting a new royal dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.27,0:20:42.34,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.70,0:20:45.79,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,One could even overtake the \Nlegitimate heir to the throne
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.26,0:20:47.76,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,and become a new monarch.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.82,0:20:50.22,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.94,0:20:54.86,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If I were to enter a spirit contract
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.86,0:20:57.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,and earn the acknowledgment of the nobles,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.71,0:20:59.73,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis wouldn't have to become queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.73,0:21:00.72,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.85,0:21:03.15,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.15,0:21:04.16,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.52,0:21:07.96,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,You declined to enter a contract, Grantz.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.61,0:21:11.59,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You were going to enter a spirit contract?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.08,0:21:14.33,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I met the requirements,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.33,0:21:15.97,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,and I didn't want to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.19,0:21:18.37,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.43,0:21:20.99,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.37,0:21:27.76,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,A spirit contract is not the wonderful thing \Nthat the people of this kingdom think it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.84,0:21:36.49,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Oh, dear. What an unpleasant \Nlook in your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.49,0:21:40.39,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm very sorry, \Nbut I would do anything to...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.07,0:21:44.87,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Your feelings are that strong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.85,0:21:48.95,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,How very, very cruel.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.43,0:21:50.92,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Lumi?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.92,0:21:53.86,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,I came here to stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.31,0:21:56.59,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,To make sure the same mistake \Nwouldn't be repeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.32,0:22:03.98,Default,Lumi,0,0,0,,Let me tell you... a certain story.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.46,0:22:04.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Ten\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Royal Succession of Resignation and Fury
